  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason includes the sure outcome (0 Euros in both cases), the differences from the sure outcome (i.e., the losses: -4000 and -3000), and the probabilities (20% and 25%). The individual considers the loss amounts and notes that the loss is '1000 Euros less' — this reflects awareness of the difference in the negative outcomes, but does not involve the weighted sum of differences. The decision reason requires a calculation of the weighted sum of differences from the sure outcome (i.e., -4000×0.20 = -800 for A, -3000×0.25 = -750 for B), and prefers the one with the less negative sum (B). The individual’s justification lacks any reference to probabilities in the weighting of differences or to the sum of weighted differences. Therefore, while the individual identifies a difference in loss magnitude, they do not apply the full rule of the decision reason. The reasoning is incomplete and simplified, missing the probabilistic weighting component essential to the reason. Thus, the decision reason was not fully used.",
